==Restrictions==
Rarity: Only [[:Category:Special Cats|Special]] and [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]]

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 106.67~120 seconds<sup>3,200f~3,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[One Horn]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>, delay 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Li'l Flying Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Flying Cat]] spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
This stage can be beaten relatively easily using [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] paired with Research [[Cat Combo]]s. Just bring either a resilient meatshield like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], or two small meatshields, and victory will be yours so long as you time them well. Courier Cat has just enough DPH at Lv.40 to knock back Rain D. every attack, effectively trivializing him; the rest of the enemies can be chipped down over time. Equip [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] to push back Li'l Flying Cat every so often.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer Cat CC]] - Despite his short range, Healer, when supported by Freeze Up Combos with the [[Sky Fruit]]/[[Blood Fruit]] treasure maxed in all chapters, can exploit One Horn and Li'l Flying Cat's traits and vulnerability to approach and perma-freeze them, essentially trivializing the stage.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] - With all the restrictions, Bahamut is one of the only available rushers able to function in the stage, having the speed and damage to cripple Owlbrow for other units to hit, and is also a serviceable counter to Rain D.

